@startuml
title ITrigger and GameEvent — board observers

skinparam linetype ortho

/'
  Previously: 15 empty marker classes implementing a raw ITrigger, with a
  Battle.runTriggers() that took no argument. Nothing could actually be
  dispatched, and an event's payload had nowhere to live.

  Now: the events are the sealed hierarchy (they carry data), and there is one
  trigger record that names the event it listens for.
'/

interface ITrigger <<sealed>> {
    - on: Class<? extends GameEvent>
    - condition: ICondition<ResolutionContext>
    - onTrigger: IAttempt

    + appliesTo(GameEvent): boolean
    + fire(ResolutionContext): AttemptResult
}

class Trigger <<record>> implements ITrigger {}

interface GameEvent <<sealed>> {
    - battle: Battle
}

/' --- turn structure --- '/
class TurnStart <<record>> implements GameEvent {
    - side: Side
}
class TurnEnd <<record>> implements GameEvent {
    - side: Side
}
class PhaseEntered <<record>> implements GameEvent {
    - phase: Phase
}

/' --- combat --- '/
class AttackDeclared <<record>> implements GameEvent {
    - attacker: PokemonInPlay
    - action: Action
}
class DamageDealt <<record>> implements GameEvent {
    - source: Optional<PokemonInPlay>
    - target: PokemonInPlay
    - amount: int
}
class Knockout <<record>> implements GameEvent {
    - knockedOut: PokemonInPlay
    - by: Optional<PokemonInPlay>
}
class Healed <<record>> implements GameEvent {
    - target: PokemonInPlay
    - amount: int
}

/' --- statuses --- '/
class StatusApplied <<record>> implements GameEvent {
    - target: PokemonInPlay
    - status: IStatus
}
class StatusRemoved <<record>> implements GameEvent {
    - target: PokemonInPlay
    - status: IStatus
}

/' --- cards --- '/
class CardPlayed <<record>> implements GameEvent {
    - side: Side
    - card: CardInstance
}
class Evolved <<record>> implements GameEvent {
    - from: PokemonCard
    - to: PokemonInPlay
}
class ToolAttached <<record>> implements GameEvent {
    - holder: PokemonInPlay
    - tool: CardInstance
}
class ToolRemoved <<record>> implements GameEvent {
    - holder: PokemonInPlay
    - tool: CardInstance
}
class Retreated <<record>> implements GameEvent {
    - from: PokemonInPlay
    - to: PokemonInPlay
}
class EnergyAttached <<record>> implements GameEvent {
    - target: PokemonInPlay
    - type: Type
}

/' --- misc --- '/
class CoinFlipped <<record>> implements GameEvent {
    - result: FlipResult
}

Trigger *-- IAttempt
ITrigger ..> GameEvent : matches

note bottom of Trigger
  **Collection, not registration.**

  Battle.collectTriggers() walks the current board on every
  dispatch — statuses, attached tools, the stadium, and passive
  abilities of everything in play — instead of subscribing and
  unsubscribing as cards enter and leave.

  A board is ~10 cards, so the cost is irrelevant, and it makes
  the whole class of stale-listener bug impossible: a Tool that
  was just discarded cannot fire, and a Pokemon that just
  evolved brings its new ability with it for free.

  Each trigger is fired with ResolutionContext.source set to its
  HOLDER and .event set to the dispatched event, so `Self`,
  `EventSource` and `EventDamage` all resolve correctly.
end note

@enduml
